-- title:
--   Complete two-dimensional local domain over a DVR is W₀[[X]]
-- statement:
--   Let $W_0$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal, and let $\varpi \in W_0$ be an element generating that maximal ideal, so $\mathfrak m_{W_0} = (\varpi)$. Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, local, Noetherian and complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$, and suppose $R$ is a $W_0$-algebra such that the composite $W_0 \to R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ of the structure map with the residue map is surjective, i.e. the residue field of $R$ is generated by the image of $W_0$. Suppose further that there is $y \in R$ with $\mathfrak m_R = (\varpi \cdot 1_R,\, y)$, the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ together with $y$, and that the Krull dimension of $R$, as an element of $\mathbb{N}^\infty$ with a bottom element adjoined, equals $2$. The conclusion is that there exists an isomorphism of $W_0$-algebras $e : W_0[[X]] \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ } R$ from the one-variable power series ring over $W_0$ onto $R$ with $e(X) = y$.
--
--   This is a Cohen-type structure statement: a complete Noetherian local domain of Krull dimension two over a complete discrete valuation ring, with residue field reached from the base and maximal ideal generated by the uniformiser together with one further element $y$, is the power series ring in $y$. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of modular curves, where stalks occurring there are identified with power series rings and then with quotients of such rings by a single relation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_powerSeries_algEquiv_apply_X_eq_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_pair_of_ringKrullDim_eq_two.lean

